# a5_qkv_head_release   (variant B line, declared 2026-09-29 from a4_threads16's own runs)
#
# impl_lever: patch_qkv_head_release.py
#   (image arion-a5_qkv_head_release_goheap.sif = shallowcopy +
#             activation_input_release + qkv_head_release; ARION_THREADS=16, GOGC=25 from the environment,
#             i.e. exactly the cumulative a4 configuration plus this lever)
# pool_attacked: host
# object_attacked: matrix.CiphertextMatricesMultiplyWeightAndAddBiasMT.func1
# (the Q/K/V ciphertext columns, bert.WeightAndAddBias in the attention)
# cost_class: free (declared)
# not_selectable_until: a4_threads16
#
# donor      MOAI-CPU m3_x_copy_release, m4_enc_ecd_x_release (free-the-consumed-input).
# mechanism  SplitCiphertextMatricesByHeads (pkg/math/matrix/matrix.go:275-290) returns sub-slices; the
#            head loop in ComputeMultiHeadAttentionMT1 (pkg/bert/attentionMT.go:61-73) keeps all
#            3 x 768 Q/K/V columns reachable; head h's columns are unread after iteration h.
# basis      a4_threads16: HWM 142,741,436 kB shared (47021870) / 142,815,708 kB exclusive (47026510).
#            Peak in the multi-head attention of both layers (plateau within 1%: L1 142.7, L0 142.4/142.2
#            M kB); bootstrap phases <= ~128 M kB. Census (136.9 M kB, 4.1% below HWM, L0 MHA):
#              WeightAndAddBias (Q/K/V)   33.8 GB  -> THIS STEP
#              RotateHoisting             32.9 GB  hoisted K/V rotations; chunking paid, unmeasured
#              Galois keys                23.9 GB  every phase; minimal keys measured PAID (+22.4%)
#              EncryptInput (ctX, L0)     12.1 GB  attention residual input, required
#              ComputeAttention parts    ~14 GB, BtsKeys 4.8, Chebyshev 4.0, runtime_retained 1.3
# order      free after paid a4 (rule 6, second case): Q/K/V not in the table before a4 moved the peak
#            into the attention.
# prediction peak -5% to -7% vs a4 (earlier at T16/GOGC 50: -7.0%, wall +0.7%); at most ~-10% (bootstrap
#            phases ~128 M kB). Refuted if <1.5% or the Q/K/V row does not shrink.
# census     SNNI_CENSUS_MIN_KB = 95,000,000.
# runs       47044191 shared (r05n01, 18 cpus, 700G). Exclusive replicate 47044193 cancelled before
#            start (no bigsmp node free).
# measured   47044191, harvested 2026-09-30: peak 131,619,236 kB (-7.8% vs a4's 142,815,504 kB); gate
#            within tolerance; LEVER|qkv_head_release|armed once per layer in markers.txt.
# census     row test not met because of the census instant: dumps only on +5% RSS; last dump
#            129.2 M kB at L1 +1,042 s (start of layer 1 MHA, no head finished); peak 131.6 M kB 837 s
#            later (~head 3), no new dump. Q/K/V row 33.8 GB as at a4 by construction.
# envelope   attention RSS maxima/minima per 250 s, layer 0:
#              a4 (exclusive and shared): maxima 127 -> 134 -> 140 -> 143 -> 144-146 GB, peak at the last heads.
#              a5: maxima to ~132 GB until head 4, then falling head by head to 115 GB; minima 124 -> 90 GB.
#            peak moved to an early head; outside the attention unchanged (L1 Bootstrap-3 131.1 vs
#            130.8 GB at a4), now 2.7% below the peak.
# cost       free by mechanism (drops references). Shared-node wall (+15.8% vs exclusive a4) carries
#            co-tenant noise; not used for typing.
